 4. 🥩 Charted: Voters&#x27; beef 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: BLS via FRED . Chart: Emily Peck/Axios If you had to pick one political advertisement to sum up voters' biggest economic beef heading into the midterms, it might have been the one about, well, beef, Axios' Emily Peck reports. 

 A viral spot for Mississippi's Democratic Senate candidate, Scott Colom, skewers a gaffe by the incumbent, Sen. Cindy Hyde‑Smith (R-Miss.), that people should simply "pick another protein" to deal with higher beef prices. (Colom is slightly ahead but the race remains too close to call .) Watch the ad ... Share this story . 

 
 
